.TH HASHLINE 1 "September 2026" "Hashline" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hashline \- a fast, quiet Markdown viewer for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hashline
.RI [ OPTIONS ] " [FILE ...]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Hashline displays Markdown in a native GTK4 window without changing the file.
With no file it opens an empty window.
If several files are supplied, it opens the first and displays a notice.
Subsequent invocations reuse the running window in the same desktop session.
Relative paths are resolved against the invoking process's working directory.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show command-line help.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the application version without opening a window.
.TP
.B \-\-
End option processing; use before file names beginning with a dash.
.SH KEYBOARD
Ctrl+O opens a file; Ctrl+F searches; Ctrl+Shift+O toggles the outline.
Ctrl++ and Ctrl+- change text size; Ctrl+0 resets it.
Ctrl+R reloads. Ctrl+A selects all; Ctrl+C copies.
Escape closes the current menu, outline or search.
.SH FILES
Preferences and recent reading positions use the GSettings schema
.BR de.kalendium.Hashline .
Documents must be UTF-8 and at most 20 MiB.
Raw HTML is displayed as text. Remote images are not loaded.
.SH EXAMPLES
.B hashline "notes/erste Datei.md"
.PP
.B hashline -- -notes.md
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gio (1),
.BR gsettings (1),
.BR xdg-mime (1)
